#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Combine every broker's order and position update streams into unified ones, and keep combining until stopped.

    bin/unified/order_updates

    redis-cli XREVRANGE unified:order-updates:stream + - COUNT 5
    redis-cli HGET unified:order-updates dhan:<order id>
    redis-cli XREVRANGE unified:positions_updates:stream + - COUNT 5
    redis-cli HGETALL unified:positions_updates

Nothing here calls a broker. Each broker's `bin/<broker>/order_updates` appends every update its websocket delivers to a
Redis Stream, as `{"timestamp", "data": <the broker's payload>}`: orders to `<broker>:order-updates:stream` (field
`update`) for dhan, flattrade, fyers, groww, indmoney, kotak, shoonya, stoxkart, wisdom_capital and zerodha, and positions to
`<broker>:positions_updates:stream` (field `position`) for the four that stream positions - fyers, groww, kotak and
wisdom_capital. Stoxkart's entries also carry the normalized `order` its script built, which is used as it is. This reads all fourteen streams as the consumer group `unified`, apart from the `persist` group the
persisters read them with, so neither disturbs the other.

**An order update** is normalized exactly as that broker's own `bin/<broker>/order_updates` normalizes it before merging
it into `<broker>:orders:orders` - the same function, carried here under a broker prefix - so its fields are the REST order
contract's: `order_id`, `exchange_order_id`, `parent_order_id`, `status`, `status_message`, `id`, `instrument_token`,
`tradingsymbol`, `exchange`, `transaction_type`, `product`, `order_type`, `validity`, the five quantities, `price`,
`trigger_price`, `average_price`, `order_timestamp`, `exchange_timestamp` and `tag`. To those it adds `broker`,
`instrument_id` and `observed_at`, the epoch the broker's script received it. It is appended to the Redis Stream
`unified:order-updates:stream` as field `update`, and the latest per order kept in the hash `unified:order-updates`,
keyed `broker:order_id`.

**A position update** is one position in the shape `bin/unified/positions` gives each position in
`unified:portfolio:positions` - the REST position contract: `instrument_id`, `symbol`, `exchange`, `segment`,
`expiry_date`, `strike_price`, `option_type`, `product` (`delivery`, `intraday`, `carry`, `margin_trading`, `cover`,
`bracket`), `quantity` (signed), `buy` and `sell` (`quantity`, `average_price`, `value`), `average_price`, `last_price`,
`pnl` (`realized`, `unrealized`, `total`), `day_change` and `day_change_percentage`. It is read by the same functions,
carried here: the update is first built into the entry the broker's script merges into `<broker>:portfolio:positions`,
keyed the same way; a Fyers or Groww update is then read from that entry's normalized `position`, and a Kotak or Wisdom
Capital one from its raw `data`, as `bin/unified/positions` reads a websocket entry. It is resolved as positions are, and
not merged with any other position. No quote is read: `last_price` and the day change come from the prices the broker
sent, which none of the four streams carries, so they are null. To the position it adds `broker`, `position_key` (the
field the broker's script keys the position by), `basis` (`day` for a Wisdom Capital `DAY:` field, `net` otherwise) and
`observed_at`. It is appended to `unified:positions_updates:stream` as field `position`, and the latest per position kept
in the hash `unified:positions_updates`, keyed `broker:position_key`.

**Resolving** follows the REST API and `bin/unified/trades`: the broker's exchange code, with the segment where the code
alone does not say the kind (Fyers, Groww, INDmoney), names an exchange and a kind of instrument; the token is looked up in
`unified:broker_tokens` and kept among that venue's segments, several survivors taken in vocabulary order, then by symbol
and id. Groww sends no token, so a Groww cash order or position is looked up by symbol in `unified:instrument_symbols`.
A position's venue is the one `bin/unified/positions` reads from it, so both resolve a position alike. Nothing
resolves to a null `instrument_id`. Answers are remembered until the cache's mapping date changes.

**Delivery.** An entry is acknowledged only after its unified stream entry and hash field are written, in one pipeline;
a failure leaves it pending in the group, and pending entries are taken first after a reconnect or at the next start, so
nothing is lost, and an entry written just before a crash may be appended twice. The consumer group is created at the
start of each stream the first time, so the first run works through everything already in them. A value that cannot be
decoded, or was trimmed from a stream while pending, is skipped and acknowledged.

**The hashes** expire at 06:00 IST, moved to the next 06:00 by every write, like the brokers' merged hashes; an update
observed before the latest 06:00 goes to the unified stream but not into the hash, so yesterday's orders do not refill
today's. The unified streams are capped at about 50,000 entries each.

Runs until Ctrl+C or SIGTERM; a Redis that cannot be reached is retried with backoff. Reads only - it places no orders.
Stoxkart streams order updates but no position updates, so its positions reach the unified documents only through
`bin/unified/positions`.
"""

